>
  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>Not a summary of the news. Two computed signals, run monthly against the full Agewell Brief archive:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Evidence maturation</strong> — which frontier vectors climbed from speculative or emerging toward contested or established, with a real gap in time between the two findings. Same-day variance across two takes on one topic doesn't count; this is about mechanisms genuinely gaining independent support over months.</li>
    <li><strong>Cross-framework convergence</strong> — historical antecedents independently cited by briefs in unrelated categories, surfacing which underlying mechanisms disparate current research is converging on without being told to look for it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Every entry links to the specific, dated brief that produced it. Nothing is inferred without a citation you can open and check yourself.</p>

  <h2>Who this is for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Longevity biotech investors who want an early, falsifiable signal on which mechanisms are gaining real support, not just press coverage.</li>
    <li>R&D teams at supplement and longevity brands scanning for where the science is actually moving before committing formulation budget.</li>
    <li>Analysts who want a sourced starting point for diligence, not a black-box AI summary.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>One issue a month, delivered by email. Each issue covers what moved since the last one — new maturation climbs, new convergence hits — plus a running methodology note so you always know exactly what's being measured and why. Monthly rather than weekly on purpose: a thin week padded to hit a schedule is worse than no issue at all, and every finding here has to earn its place by actually happening in the archive.</p>

  <h2>Price</h2>
  <p>$399/month, or $3,990/year. No trial, no self-serve checkout yet — every subscription starts as a conversation so the first issue actually reflects what you're trying to track.</p>

  <div class="radar-callout">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start a conversation</p>
    <a href="mailto:hello@agewellbrief.com?subject=Research%20Radar%20inquiry">hello@agewellbrief.com</a>
    <p class="radar-callout-note">Tell us what you're tracking — a mechanism, a category, a competitor's pipeline — and we'll send a sample issue built from the live archive before you commit to anything.</p>
  </div>
</InfoPage>

